=== DIAGNOSIS ===
is_anomaly: false
faulty_devices: none
diagnosis_text:
The network is fully operational at the time of investigation. Every
component that the helpdesk ticket claims to be broken was verified and
found healthy.

The inter-router link (router1:eth0 ↔ router2:eth0, subnet 193.10.11.0/24)
is physically UP on both ends with correct IP addresses (193.10.11.1 and
193.10.11.2). The eBGP session between AS 1 (router1) and AS 2 (router2) is
in the Established state, has been continuously up since lab start with zero
drops, and is exchanging prefixes correctly: router1 receives 200.1.1.0/24
from router2 and router2 receives 195.11.14.0/24 from router1. Both routes
are installed in the FIB as the selected best path. The host default gateways
are correct (pc1 → 195.11.14.1, pc2 → 200.1.1.1). A live end-to-end ICMP
test from pc1 (195.11.14.2) to pc2 (200.1.1.2) returned 4/4 packets with
zero loss and sub-2 ms RTT. The FRR log shows only normal keepalive
exchanges; the single early "nexthop_set failed" line is a harmless transient
TCP connection attempt logged before the session completed handshake.

Root cause: There is no fault. The operations team's assertion that "the line
between the two buildings went down" is incorrect; the link and the BGP
session are working normally.

Corrective action: No configuration or hardware change is needed. Inform the
operations team that the inter-site path is healthy and ask them to recheck
the application layer (order-exchange service, DNS resolution, firewall rules
on the endpoint hosts) for the real source of the reported outage.
=== END ===
